	  <td class="legend">
	    <a href="index.html#Table_001"><i>Table 1</i></a>:
	    <br />
	    The subset of Warsaw basis operators considered in this work, following the definitions of [1,none]. Repeated indices are summed over. These purely bosonic operators are independent of the flavour symmetry imposed on the SMEFT Lagrangian. The symbol $ H $ refers to the Higgs doublet; $ D_\mu $ is a covariant derivative and $ \square = D^\mu D_\mu $ the d'Alembert operator; $ W^i_{\mu\nu} $ and $ B_{\mu\nu} $ are the $ \mathrm{SU}(2)_L $ and $ \mathrm{U}(1)_Y $ field strength tensors; $ i,j,k $ are $ \mathrm{SU}(2) $ adjoint indices. 
	  </td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
	  <!-- td class="table" width="50%" -->
	  <td class="table" id="Table_002">
	    <a href="CMS-PAS-SMP-25-002_Table_002.png">
